				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1001088#post-2116910</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1001088/anabasis-hub#post-2116910</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 24 Sep 2014 00:21:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>ensimismada</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1451590</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Is that Spanish at the bottom of the background supposed to be&#8230; muddled? Because if <em>pendejos</em> is a noun of direct address, it's not in agreement with how <em>ir</em> was conjugated. That is, <em>pendejos</em> is plural and <em>vas</em> is the singular second person conjugation. Also, the construction is <em>ir + a</em> + infinitive. Also-also, if you're using &quot;to see&quot; to mean &quot;to understand,&quot; you want <em>ver</em>, not <em>mirar.</em></p> <p>If you're trying to say &quot;Do you see now what you'll do with the Anabasis, fools?&quot; I would use <em>¿Ahora ven lo que van a hacer con el anabasis, pendejos?</em> This construction still seems bulky to me (I'm not a native speaker), but it's definitely clearer.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
